68
00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.420
Jim sits down too.

69
00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:13.220
She has blown past the little kiss, but he is still blushing and very aware of it.

70
00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.160
Oh my gosh.

71
00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.240
That is not how I remember it.

72
00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.740
That is in the shooting draft.

73
00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.140
And now when you watch the episode, Pam kisses Michael on the cheek, still leaves him speechless.

74
00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:32.880
But it says Pam impulsively grabs Jim and kisses him.

75
00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.040
So I'm just saying.

76
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:35.880
Okay.

77
00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:36.860
Okay.

78
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.120
I know we can still debate it, but I feel like that does support my argument.

79
00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.160
All right.

80
00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.360
Well, I might stand corrected.

81
00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.580
Oh, you're starting to sway me.

82
00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.380
I have to say.

83
00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:59.800
Well, in this episode, I very confidently share that the person at the end of this episode

84
00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:05.760
who plays the Chili's manager that bans Pam from coming back to Chili's, I say that this

85
00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.380
