252
00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:39.410
Aw, Greg.

253
00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:42.310
This leads me into fast fact number two.

254
00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:48.010
The Dundies was the story that Greg wanted to use as the season one, episode one pilot.

255
00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.210
Instead of?

256
00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.610
Instead of the pilot.

257
00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:51.070
Yes.

258
00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:56.350
This was his idea for how to kick off the American version of the office, but the network said

259
00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:58.990
they preferred we do an adaptation of the British pilot.

260
00:11:59.270 --> 00:11:59.790
Wow.

261
00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:01.950
And Greg was very, very disappointed.

262
00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:08.150
But if you notice, and Angela, maybe you did notice, there has been a Dundie on Michael's

263
00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:09.450
desk from the very beginning.

264
00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:14.690
It's in our opening credits, and Michael Scott, all through season one, had a Dundie.

265
00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:18.430
It's in the opening credits, but is it on his desk in the episode?

266
00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:19.250
Oh, well, now that I don't know.

267
00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:23.510
See, because I don't think it's on his actual desk, but I think it's in the credits.

268
00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:24.490
It's in the credits.

269
00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:24.790
Yes.

270
00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:29.950
But I do think that even that little bit is that way where Greg had something in his

271
00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:30.290
head.

272
00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:30.630
Right.

273
00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:37.090
He had this idea of these Dundie Awards looming for all this time, and finally, when we got

274
00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.730
picked up, he was able to do something with it.

275
00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.390
Well, thank goodness we got a second season.

276
00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.950
That would really have been a bummer.

277
00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:45.110
Or else that little shot in the opening credits would have remained a mystery.

278
00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:46.570
What is the little man on his desk?

279
00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:47.810
What's the little man with the briefcase?

280
00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:48.630
What is it?

281
00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.430
Are we ready for fast fact number three?

282
00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.530
We're moving more quickly than I thought we would.

283
00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:54.330
Well, let me just tell you, I'm just letting you go.

284
00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:55.190
All right.

285
00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.810
Jenna, I wish you guys could see her.

286
00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:58.970
She came in what looks like a mechanic's outfit.

287
00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:00.830
Yeah, it's my green jumpsuit.

288
00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:01.550
Her green jumpsuit.

289
00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:02.530
But I also have a hat on.

290
00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:03.030
A hat on.

291
00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.390
It's like she came to play.

292
00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.450
Either that or pilot an airplane.

293
00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:07.490
But you are ready.

294
00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:08.750
Do you need anything assembled?

295
00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:10.870
Because I think I look like I could assemble something.

296
00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:11.490
Maybe.

297
00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.490
Okay, go, go, go.

298
00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:14.150
All right, fast fact number three.

299
00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:18.510
The second season of The Office was originally only six episodes long.

300
00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.050
We only got picked up for six episodes.

301
00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:20.670
I know.

302
00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.190
We were so excited to get six.

303
00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:24.350
But after that, we're like, well, I guess that's it.

304
00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:25.490
We, that might be all.

305
00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:26.810
But they started airing.

306
00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.590
And then they ordered three more.

307
00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.370
Then they ordered four more.

308
00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:30.830
Right.

309
00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.190
Then I think they ordered the rest of the whole season.

310
00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:35.990
And we ended up with a usual amount of time.

311
00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:38.090
Yeah, but in the beginning, we were like, well, we got six.

312
00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:38.730
Well, that's that.

313
00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.010
Oh, no, we got, we got three more.

314
00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:44.090
Oh, we got, you know, it was, it kind of gave you that sense of like, well, we might as

315
00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:47.170
well go for it because we don't know if we're going to have this job.

316
00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:47.550
Yeah.

317
00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:52.410
And this episode of The Dundies was actually the third episode that we shot when we came

318
00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:52.730
back.

319
00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:57.410
And it was the first episode that we ever shot away from our office set.

320
00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:57.790
Yes.

321
00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.470
This is the first time we went on a completely different location.

322
00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.070
It was really, really cool.

323
00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:09.010
And we shot this the week after Steve Carell's movie, The 40-Year-Old Virgin, hit theaters.

324
00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:09.810
Yes.

325
00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.570
It was the number one movie at the box office.

326
00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:13.790
We were so excited for him.

327
00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:18.470
And Steve being the sweetheart that he is, invited the whole entire cast to the premiere.

328
00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:18.970
Yeah.

329
00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:20.730
And we all went, we got dressed up.

330
00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:25.450
And that was like one of the first fancy movie anything parties I've ever been to.

331
00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.510
I have a crazy story about that, Angela.

332
00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:27.710
What?

333
00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:30.050
Well, we had been shooting all day.

334
00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.770
And then the premiere was that night.

335
00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:32.150
Yeah.

336
00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:34.490
And we got dressed on set.

337
00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:36.610
And the hair and makeup people did our hair and makeup.

338
00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:36.870
Yeah.

339
00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.070
And we carpooled.

340
00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:40.090
And we went to this premiere.

341
00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:44.310
And when we got there, I was wearing this dress.

342
00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.930
It's very hard to explain.

343
00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:48.390
Maybe we can find a photo of it and put it on our website.

344
00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:53.090
It was sort of like a lacy mermaid thing.

345
00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:56.450
It was like green and blue.

346
00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:57.150
What?

347
00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.530
I don't even remember where I got it or how I got it.

348
00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:03.170
But it was my first big movie premiere.

349
00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:03.610
Right.

350
00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:06.990
I didn't know what you were supposed to wear or how you were supposed to dress.

351
00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:10.170
It was a silky dress.

352
00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:13.270
And then over it had a lace part.

353
00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:14.830
So, the silk part was like the slip.

354
00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:16.410
And then the lace part went over.

355
00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:17.430
A silk slip.

356
00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:18.350
Thank you, Angela.

357
00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:22.330
And it was blue and green sort of mermaid-y colors, I guess.

358
00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:22.850
Oh, well.

359
00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:28.330
And it had this really big ribbon around the hips.

360
00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:29.050
Okay.

361
00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:29.910
What is happening?

362
00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:30.970
But I'll tell you.

363
00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:34.710
And then it had the ribbon tassels were hanging down in the front.

364
00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:34.930
In the front.

365
00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:35.310
Okay?

366
00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:35.670
Okay.

367
00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.490
So, when we got to the premiere, I had to pee so badly.

368
00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:44.290
So, before we walked the red carpet, I ran into the bathroom and I peed very quickly.

369
00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:45.550
Did you pee on the ribbon?

370
00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:46.850
I did not pee on the ribbon.

371
00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:47.150
Okay.

372
00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:48.630
No, that would have been awful.

373
00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:50.090
That's where I thought the story was going.

374
00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.810
No, the ribbon did not dip in the toilet.

375
00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:52.230
Okay.

376
00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:54.150
But, you know, that happens sometimes.

377
00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.270
Yeah, I said that because I feel like it's happened to me.

378
00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:59.450
Okay, I did not pee on the ribbon, but I was rushing.

379
00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:02.890
And I came back out and I went to the red carpet.

380
00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:04.090
I took my pictures.

381
00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.050
I posed.

382
00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:06.130
I did the pictures.

383
00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:06.970
Whirlwind.

384
00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:08.270
Hoped I did it right.

385
00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:09.470
Went inside.

386
00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:15.810
When I got inside, I realized that I had tucked the slip into my underwear.

387
00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:16.390
No!

388
00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:17.570
And I had—

389
00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:20.090
Was your butt showing in the lace in the photos?

390
00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:22.110
No, my butt was not showing.

391
00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:28.270
Thankfully, that ribbon was strategically poised to cover my lady bits.

392
00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:29.190
Oh, Jenna.

393
00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:37.440
Because it was just lace on the bottom because I had tucked the slip into my underwear.

394
00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:38.600
But it gets worse.

395
00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:39.240
What?

396
00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:41.420
How can it get worse than you tucked your—

397
00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:45.480
Also, didn't you feel some air in places you should have been feeling air?

398
00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:46.880
I was so nervous.

399
00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:47.540
You were rushing.

400
00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:48.560
You were rushing.

401
00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:49.320
Okay, okay, okay.

402
00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:52.200
I wanted to get into my friend Steve's big movie premiere.

403
00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.520
Okay, how does it get worse?

404
00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:58.700
You know when you go and you buy, like, the three-pack of cotton underwear at Target?

405
00:16:58.900 --> 00:16:59.440
All the time.

406
00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:04.420
And there's a white pair, a black pair, a new pair, and then a crazy-colored pair?

407
00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:06.900
I was wearing the crazy pair.

408
00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:07.920
Oh, Jenna.

409
00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:10.760
From my Target underwear pack.

410
00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:15.500
And I think, like, from the back, you must have been able to see it.

411
00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:17.780
Thankfully, I didn't turn around on the red carpet.

412
00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:21.100
But I'm sure many people saw that as I was walking.

413
00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.940
Jenna, I do not remember if I did the red carpet or not.

414
00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:25.100
I don't know if I did.

415
00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.200
I think I just went in the theater.

416
00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:31.500
I mean, I would have to go back and look, but I feel like I didn't even know that we had to do that.

417
00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:33.320
Someone made me do it.

418
00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:37.220
Like, I got out of the car and, you know, someone grabbed me and said,

419
00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:38.260
you need to take pictures.

420
00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:39.300
And I was—

421
00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:43.340
I'm pretty sure I drove myself and I just parked in the garage and I walked in.

422
00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:47.100
But I just remember being so excited for Steve.

423
00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:49.100
And he was so happy we were there.

424
00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:53.020
He had us all sitting together and he came over and he gave us all a big hug.

425
00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:55.220
And I kind of remember that he wore a white suit.

426
00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.400
Am I remembering that right?

427
00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:56.880
Don't know.

428
00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:57.400
Don't know.

429
00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.300
Should have looked it up.

430
00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.020
We were doing the dundies today.

431
00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:02.120
I don't think I bought anything new.

432
00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:03.500
I don't remember what I wore.

433
00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:08.940
I sat between John and Rain at the premiere when the movie was over.

434
00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.720
I turned to John and I said,

435
00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:15.660
Steve is going to be the biggest movie star when this movie comes out.

436
00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:15.940
Yeah.

437
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.100
He's going to stop being Steve.

438
00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:18.980
He's going to start being Steve Carell.

439
00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:20.020
Yeah.

440
00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:23.040
And it's going to be weird because we know Steve.

441
00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:23.600
Right.

442
00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:27.740
And the rest of the world is going to know Steve Carell in about one week.

443
00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:30.940
I remember thinking like, holy moly, this is going to be a big hit.

444
00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.780
So now we're shooting the dundies.

445
00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:33.280
Yes.

446
00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.300
The 40-year-old virgin has come out.

447
00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.520
And as predicted, Steve is Steve Carell.

448
00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:39.780
He's a huge movie star.

449
00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:44.360
And since we're on location, they had to economize space.

450
00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:47.460
And we were each given these teeny, teeny, tiny trailers.

451
00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:48.960
To change clothes in, basically.

452
00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:49.540
That's right.

453
00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:50.260
That's all you could do.

454
00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.000
That's all you could do.

455
00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.100
It was about the size of a closet.

456
00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:54.700
Even Steve, biggest movie star in the country,

457
00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.840
did not get a larger closet to change in.

458
00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:59.940
And his was infested with ants.

459
00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:00.500
Ew.

460
00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:07.540
And I will just never forget how humble he was and how he did not complain at all.

461
00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:09.440
And I thought, you know what?

462
00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:11.920
That is how you behave with class.

463
00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:12.420
Yes.

464
00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:12.520
Yes.

465
00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:14.060
And Steve is not a complainer.

466
00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:15.160
And he's professional.

467
00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:16.260
And he's on time.

468
00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:18.180
And he gets his shiitake done.

469
00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:20.020
And he even joked about it.

470
00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:23.720
He was like, well, that's how they keep you humble in this business.

471
00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:26.500
It was great.

472
00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:27.520
It was so great.

473
00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:30.020
I have a fourth fast fact, Angela.

474
00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:32.620
But Jenna, you only do three fast facts.

475
00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:33.580
But this is the Dundies.

476
00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:35.900
The Dundies deserves a fourth fast fact.

477
00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:36.340
Okay.

478
00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:43.740
So fast fact number four, and this was based on a lot of questions from fans about the Chili's location.

479
00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.200
It was not a real Chili's.

480
00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:48.160
In fact, it was an out-of-business restaurant.

481
00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:52.080
We got permission from Chili's to make it a Chili's.

482
00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:56.900
And they sent all their gear, all their signs and their chalkboard stuff to make it look like a Chili's.

483
00:19:56.900 --> 00:20:08.060
Yes, they spent weeks, Michael Gallenberg, our set designer, spent weeks conferring with Chili's, reconstructing with painstaking detail this Chili's restaurant,

484
00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:11.200
which was in an abandoned former restaurant.

485
00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.920
It was in an abandoned restaurant in an empty parking lot.

486
00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:17.060
And it, I mean, it didn't even have any signs or anything on it when they started.

487
00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.180
It was just an out-of-business restaurant.

488
00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:19.780
Yeah.

489
00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:21.280
So there you go, guys.

490
00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:25.520
You can't, and what's crazy about that is you can't go eat at that Chili's.

491
00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:30.700
It is near a mall, and on my lunch break, I wanted a mask and snorkel, and I went.

492
00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:31.460
What?

493
00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:34.100
Yeah, so this is a story that's not that interesting.

494
00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:42.300
But when we filmed, listen, we filmed at this random neighborhood at this out-of-business restaurant, and I just happened to see that it was near, like, a mall,

495
00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:44.980
and I was able on my lunch break to get a snorkel and a mask.

496
00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:46.020
For what reason?

497
00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.560
I wanted to go snorkeling.

498
00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:48.860
I was going to go.

499
00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:52.160
But this is what I remember about this restaurant.

500
00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:53.320
It's like, oh, that's the restaurant.

501
00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:54.060
Snorkeling where?

502
00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.160
It's like the ocean, Jenna.

503
00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:58.140
I was going to go to Catalina Island.

504
00:20:58.320 --> 00:20:59.600
Listen, the details aren't important.

505
00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:06.760
What is important is when I think about that out-of-business restaurant that we filmed in as a Chili's is that that's near where I bought my mask and snorkel.

506
00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:08.520
Do you still have your mask and snorkel?

507
00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:09.000
It broke.

508
00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:10.120
Here's the thing, guys.

