1211
00:47:39.910 --> 00:47:42.650
I can't look at myself rolling my eyes at myself.

1212
00:47:42.810 --> 00:47:48.630
So now we get into the tender moment where Michael is desperately trying to keep the Dundies

1213
00:47:48.630 --> 00:47:51.750
going and the guys at the bar start to heckle him.

1214
00:47:51.870 --> 00:47:52.170
Yeah.

1215
00:47:52.170 --> 00:47:54.450
And he's so wounded.

1216
00:47:55.370 --> 00:47:57.310
And Pam won't have it.

1217
00:47:57.630 --> 00:47:59.130
Well, I think it's that moment.

1218
00:47:59.310 --> 00:48:05.690
Even there's a look that comes across Jim's face of like, ooh, like that's mean, you know?

1219
00:48:05.870 --> 00:48:06.010
Yeah.

1220
00:48:06.090 --> 00:48:10.790
And it's sort of that thing of like, you know, your creepy cousin that creeps everyone out,

1221
00:48:10.930 --> 00:48:12.950
but you have to take up for them because they're your cousin.

1222
00:48:12.990 --> 00:48:17.930
It's like that moment of like, okay, he's like family and we get to like make fun of him,

1223
00:48:18.010 --> 00:48:18.770
but no one else can.

1224
00:48:18.770 --> 00:48:19.550
That's right.

1225
00:48:19.810 --> 00:48:25.230
And Pam starts chanting Dundies and getting people to rally around him.

1226
00:48:25.430 --> 00:48:26.770
And I love that.

1227
00:48:26.930 --> 00:48:29.930
And this is a little bit the relationship between Pam and Michael.

1228
00:48:30.290 --> 00:48:35.390
This is the way that she shows up for him, the way he shows up for her at her art show later.

1229
00:48:35.570 --> 00:48:35.750
Yeah.

1230
00:48:36.410 --> 00:48:39.250
Like in their lowest moments, they are there for one another.

1231
00:48:39.250 --> 00:48:43.750
When Pam gives him a hug, when she gets her Dundie, his face is so precious.

1232
00:48:44.050 --> 00:48:47.050
He's just like, it's like the whole night was made in that moment.

1233
