when you say, I'd like to thank God for this Dundie, it cuts to Jim.

1240
00:49:05.550 --> 00:49:10.890
And Jim's reaction to you thanking God for your Dundie is one of the best moments for me of the

1241
00:49:10.890 --> 00:49:11.510
whole episode.

1242
00:49:11.650 --> 00:49:13.170
It is just so sweet.

1243
00:49:13.270 --> 00:49:17.510
He's just looking at you like, oh, my sweet little drunk friend.

1244
00:49:17.570 --> 00:49:18.390
I love you.

1245
00:49:18.390 --> 00:49:23.830
Well, I talked to Mindy about this on the day, and she had told me that Greg did not

1246
00:49:23.830 --> 00:49:27.790
have total confidence in Pam thanking God for her Dundie, but we were going to do it

1247
00:49:27.790 --> 00:49:28.090
anyway.

1248
00:49:28.370 --> 00:49:30.270
He was a little bit like, I don't totally get it.

1249
00:49:30.290 --> 00:49:36.010
And she's like, no, you know, like whenever people win awards or they have like big sports

1250
00:49:36.010 --> 00:49:38.290
