1251
00:49:38.410 --> 00:49:40.110
And I asked her, I said, but how do I do it?

1252
00:49:40.170 --> 00:49:42.510
Because, and she said, you do it totally sincerely.

1253
00:49:42.850 --> 00:49:43.070
Yeah.

1254
00:49:43.210 --> 00:49:48.250
She's like, you really are like sincerely thankful and grateful for your Dundie tonight.

1255
00:49:48.250 --> 00:49:52.410
Totally made sense to me because I felt like drunk Pam thinks this is what you do when

1256
00:49:52.410 --> 00:49:52.990
you win an award.

1257
00:49:53.190 --> 00:49:53.370
That's right.

1258
00:49:53.450 --> 00:49:56.570
You take a moment, you thank God, then you scream.

1259
00:49:56.690 --> 00:49:57.030
Woohoo!

1260
00:49:57.350 --> 00:49:57.690
Yeah.

1261
00:49:57.990 --> 00:49:59.330
And I loved it so much.

1262
00:49:59.490 --> 00:50:06.450
And then after this, after she gets her Dundie, Pam kisses Jim on the lips.

1263
00:50:06.670 --> 00:50:07.270
I know.

1264
00:50:07.470 --> 00:50:07.970
I know.

1265
00:50:08.070 --> 00:50:08.790
Was that weird?

1266
00:50:09.150 --> 00:50:10.970
Well, this was a big fan question.

1267
00:50:11.170 --> 00:50:16.090
Caitlin asked, do you consider this episode as Pam and Jim's first kiss?

1268
00:50:16.110 --> 00:50:18.110
Or do you think it's casino night?

1269
00:50:18.770 --> 00:50:21.490
I did not consider this their first kiss.

1270
00:50:21.610 --> 00:50:22.170
I did.

1271
00:50:22.470 --> 00:50:23.090
John did.

1272
00:50:23.330 --> 00:50:24.070
I disagree.

1273
00:50:24.470 --> 00:50:27.330
I consider it, you planted one on him.

1274
00:50:27.870 --> 00:50:31.250
The intention there was that it was accidental.

1275
00:50:31.770 --> 00:50:35.130
The intention was that Pam was going for his cheek.

1276
00:50:35.270 --> 00:50:35.610
Uh-huh.

1277
00:50:35.770 --> 00:50:42.210
And it was one of those moments where you, he moved his head in a way that I wasn't expecting

1278
00:50:42.210 --> 00:50:44.850
and I'm drunk and I just followed through.

1279
00:50:45.130 --> 00:50:47.610
That was what was in my head as Pam.

1280
00:50:47.810 --> 00:50:50.970
So I wasn't thinking that I was intending to kiss his lips.

1281
00:50:51.170 --> 00:50:53.910
And so Pam kind of doesn't register it.

1282
00:50:54.170 --> 00:50:54.950
That was me.

1283
00:50:55.470 --> 00:51:00.730
John said that Jim, who is not drunk, was very aware that they just kissed on the lips.

1284
00:51:00.830 --> 00:51:03.290
And this was a whole conversation that we had off camera.

1285
00:51:03.490 --> 00:51:04.590
I agree with him, though.

1286
00:51:04.690 --> 00:51:05.630
And I see both sides.

1287
00:51:05.630 --> 00:51:09.150
I see as a drunk person, you just kind of hug and you're a little sloppy.

1288
00:51:09.670 --> 00:51:14.250
But I see for him as a sober person, this person he's in love with just kissed him.

1289
00:51:15.070 --> 00:51:15.510
Yeah.

1290
00:51:15.510 --> 00:51:18.030
But it was unintentional on Pam's part.

1291
00:51:18.130 --> 00:51:18.490
I know.

1292
00:51:18.530 --> 00:51:19.430
In her mind.

1293
00:51:19.590 --> 00:51:19.990
I know.

1294
00:51:20.150 --> 00:51:25.090
But a lot of people wrote in and said, oh, my gosh, why didn't everyone in the office,

1295
00:51:25.230 --> 00:51:28.130
why wasn't this a big gossipy moment?

1296
00:51:28.130 --> 00:51:31.490
They know Pam's engaged and they all witnessed her kiss Jim.

1297
00:51:31.970 --> 00:51:36.730
And in my mind, it was because it wasn't really a kiss.

1298
00:51:36.870 --> 00:51:37.610
It wasn't a...

1299
00:51:38.190 --> 00:51:41.490
Oh, well, in my mind, everyone was talking about it at work.

1300
00:51:41.590 --> 00:51:41.830
Oh.

1301
00:51:42.110 --> 00:51:42.370
Trust me.

1302
00:51:43.150 --> 00:51:48.390
Because I tell you what, Angela Martin was sitting with Phyllis in a booth when that happened.

1303
00:51:48.630 --> 00:51:50.610
And I'm pretty sure she was like, mm-hmm.

1304
00:51:50.890 --> 00:51:53.110
Did you see the office mattress?

1305
00:51:53.410 --> 00:51:55.550
Just to smooch someone else.

1306
00:51:55.730 --> 00:51:57.870
Well, I have another fan question for you then.

1307
00:51:58.070 --> 00:51:59.070
This one is from Amy.

1308
00:51:59.470 --> 00:52:05.870
She said, at the end, when you drive Pam home, in my mind, Angela would be so disgusted

1309
00:52:05.870 --> 00:52:08.850
by Pam's behavior, it seems odd that she would give her a ride.

1310
00:52:08.970 --> 00:52:11.910
Well, let me tell you, Amy, if you watch the deleted scenes,

1311
00:52:11.910 --> 00:52:17.970
because I did, you will see that Angela Martin has a talking head where she is the company's

1312
00:52:17.970 --> 00:52:19.070
designated driver.

1313
00:52:19.850 --> 00:52:24.190
And you would know that Angela Martin would take this very serious as the safety officer

1314
00:52:24.190 --> 00:52:25.590
for Dunder Mifflin.

1315
00:52:25.750 --> 00:52:28.590
And I have this talking head where Angela goes on to say,

1316
00:52:28.750 --> 00:52:29.470
and you know what?

1317
00:52:29.610 --> 00:52:31.310
No one gives me any gas money.

1318
00:52:31.450 --> 00:52:33.210
And everyone lives all over.

1319
00:52:33.470 --> 00:52:34.550
It's very expensive.

1320
00:52:36.050 --> 00:52:37.790
Wow, that is gold.

1321
00:52:38.010 --> 00:52:39.690
So she's always the martyr.

1322
00:52:39.870 --> 00:52:42.350
She's doing her job, but no one gives her gas money.

1323
00:52:42.450 --> 00:52:45.450
And she has to drive these drunks around, but she's the designated driver.

1324
00:52:45.450 --> 00:52:46.930
And so she has to do it.

1325
00:52:47.030 --> 00:52:50.190
So not only did Pam probably not give her any gas money.

1326
00:52:50.350 --> 00:52:50.730
Yeah.

1327
00:52:51.110 --> 00:52:55.030
She was very disappointed in her behavior.

1328
00:52:55.270 --> 00:52:59.290
Angela quietly judged her the whole drive and probably told her, you need to make some

1329
00:52:59.290 --> 00:53:00.490
new life choices.

1330
00:53:00.490 --> 00:53:03.210
Amy also wanted to know, was that really you driving?

1331
00:53:03.530 --> 00:53:04.550
Yes, it was.

1332
00:53:04.670 --> 00:53:08.050
At 20 minutes, two seconds in the car, you see my shoulder.

1333
00:53:08.430 --> 00:53:09.710
Now, here's the thing.

1334
00:53:09.810 --> 00:53:11.310
They wanted me every time in the car.

1335
00:53:11.470 --> 00:53:13.190
You got in with me every time I pulled away.

1336
00:53:13.330 --> 00:53:16.210
And then I would back up and we'd do the scene over a few times.

1337
00:53:16.490 --> 00:53:22.010
And I had a front row seat watching Pam and Jim have that sort of very tender but awkward

1338
00:53:22.010 --> 00:53:25.990
moment where Pam has a question for him, but then notices the camera.

1339
00:53:26.130 --> 00:53:29.070
I watched that whole thing over and over as you guys did it.

1340
00:53:29.130 --> 00:53:29.950
And it was so great.

1341
00:53:29.950 --> 00:53:31.590
You guys did such a fantastic job.

1342
00:53:31.790 --> 00:53:36.250
And when I rewatched it, part of me was like, well, why'd they have me in the car?

1343
00:53:36.370 --> 00:53:37.750
You don't see me anyway.

1344
00:53:38.170 --> 00:53:39.150
But they didn't know.

1345
00:53:39.270 --> 00:53:42.270
As you know, with our show, we always had an A camera and a B camera.

1346
00:53:42.410 --> 00:53:44.570
And they would be sort of carving up the scene.

1347
00:53:44.690 --> 00:53:47.630
And there might be this moment where they whipped around and could have seen me.

1348
00:53:47.790 --> 00:53:50.530
So they wanted to make sure I was there just in case.

1349
00:53:50.710 --> 00:53:52.150
And I was happy to be there.

1350
00:53:52.490 --> 00:53:53.890
But also, I had...

1351
00:53:53.890 --> 00:53:57.290
A lot of times they would use a double for that in other shows.

1352
00:53:57.290 --> 00:53:59.670
But in our show, we were our own doubles.

1353
00:53:59.930 --> 00:54:00.270
That's right.

1354
00:54:00.290 --> 00:54:04.470
Because as a documentary, you really never knew where that second camera would end up landing.

1355
00:54:04.470 --> 00:54:05.890
And you could end up on camera.

1356
00:54:06.030 --> 00:54:12.090
I was asked, is that a cat air freshener hanging from your rear view mirror in your car?

1357
00:54:12.470 --> 00:54:13.050
Is it?

1358
00:54:13.050 --> 00:54:15.730
It looks like it could be a cat or a tree.

1359
00:54:15.910 --> 00:54:16.730
Guys, I don't know.

1360
00:54:16.910 --> 00:54:17.990
I tried to zoom in on it.

1361
00:54:18.030 --> 00:54:19.170
Oh, I hope it's a cat.

1362
00:54:19.250 --> 00:54:19.930
I hope it's a green...

1363
00:54:19.930 --> 00:54:20.890
Let's call it a cat.

1364
00:54:20.890 --> 00:54:21.950
I hope it's a green cat.

1365
00:54:21.950 --> 00:54:24.470
A green cat doesn't sound right now, Angela.

1366
00:54:24.650 --> 00:54:25.110
I know.

1367
00:54:25.270 --> 00:54:28.270
But maybe it was a Christmas cat that I held on to.

1368
00:54:28.610 --> 00:54:29.150
Not sure.

1369
00:54:29.550 --> 00:54:34.610
Something we haven't talked about is the scene where Pam falls off the stool because she is so drunk.

1370
00:54:35.490 --> 00:54:37.810
And this leads me into a fan question.

1371
00:54:38.390 --> 00:54:42.270
Matt Sheldon asked, how did you get Chili's to cooperate with this idea?

1372
00:54:43.070 --> 00:54:44.830
Well, they were on the fence.

1373
00:54:44.830 --> 00:54:47.590
And we almost weren't allowed to film there, remember?

1374
00:54:47.850 --> 00:54:49.210
Well, here's what happened.

1375
00:54:49.990 --> 00:54:54.070
Originally, in the script, Pam vomits all over the bar.

1376
00:54:54.210 --> 00:54:55.630
She does not fall off the stool.

1377
00:54:55.790 --> 00:54:56.690
She is listening to Jim.

1378
00:54:56.770 --> 00:54:57.510
She is nodding.

1379
00:54:57.630 --> 00:54:58.550
And then she vomits.

1380
00:54:58.990 --> 00:55:01.150
And we had been filming for two days.

1381
00:55:01.370 --> 00:55:01.750
Right.

1382
00:55:01.970 --> 00:55:06.090
And I guess suddenly they had had Chili's permission.

1383
00:55:06.330 --> 00:55:07.810
Chili's helped build the Chili's.

1384
00:55:07.950 --> 00:55:11.630
And someone at Chili's read the script, finally.

1385
00:55:11.830 --> 00:55:12.470
Well, I guess...

1386
00:55:12.470 --> 00:55:13.590
And freaked out.

1387
00:55:13.790 --> 00:55:15.750
I read the script wasn't fully complete.

1388
00:55:16.010 --> 00:55:17.570
You know, they hadn't done their second pass.

1389
00:55:17.710 --> 00:55:20.290
And so Chili's had not gotten all of the scenes.

1390
00:55:20.450 --> 00:55:24.930
And so they didn't have the scene where Pam vomited and all of this happened.

1391
00:55:25.090 --> 00:55:27.810
Well, once they read that, they shut down the production.

1392
00:55:28.110 --> 00:55:28.450
Yes.

1393
00:55:28.570 --> 00:55:29.430
And we thought, what?

1394
00:55:29.530 --> 00:55:30.970
They said, no way.

1395
00:55:31.190 --> 00:55:31.590
Mm-mm.

1396
00:55:31.590 --> 00:55:38.270
We, they were very nervous about the drinking and the drunkenness and the sort of way that

1397
00:55:38.270 --> 00:55:39.670
that might reflect on Chili's.

1398
00:55:39.810 --> 00:55:42.830
So Greg and Mindy started scrambling.

1399
00:55:43.170 --> 00:55:48.770
And they came up with this idea that instead of vomiting, that Pam would fall off a stool.

1400
00:55:48.770 --> 00:55:49.450
Right.

1401
00:55:49.610 --> 00:55:52.870
And then also, I think it was Rain's idea to say, well, maybe Dwight could say, oh, she's

1402
00:55:52.870 --> 00:55:55.130
had a seizure and not the vomiting.

1403
00:55:55.450 --> 00:56:01.530
And then the other part of it was that we had to write in a new element, which is that

1404
00:56:01.530 --> 00:56:03.650
Pam was going to get banned from Chili's.

1405
00:56:04.010 --> 00:56:10.670
And the person who gives the speech in the episode was an actual Chili's manager franchise

1406
00:56:10.670 --> 00:56:12.370
owner named John Bossert.

1407
00:56:12.570 --> 00:56:12.850
Mm-hmm.

1408
00:56:12.870 --> 00:56:14.150
He was not an actor.

1409
00:56:14.650 --> 00:56:14.770
Right.

1410
00:56:14.770 --> 00:56:20.930
And they felt like by having an actual Chili's representative state very clearly the Chili's

1411
00:56:20.930 --> 00:56:22.690
policy against over-serving.

1412
00:56:22.830 --> 00:56:23.110
Right.

1413
00:56:23.290 --> 00:56:27.910
And banning Pam for life, then they allowed us to film the rest of the episode.

1414
00:56:28.050 --> 00:56:28.330
Yes.

1415
00:56:28.450 --> 00:56:31.370
And also, they had Pam, they had you as Pam.

1416
00:56:31.770 --> 00:56:34.210
A waiter never brought you more drinks.

1417
00:56:34.210 --> 00:56:36.330
You were reaching on other people's tables.

1418
00:56:36.330 --> 00:56:38.590
So you were doing it, not Chili's.

1419
00:56:38.690 --> 00:56:39.530
And you know what?

1420
00:56:39.530 --> 00:56:40.310
I think that's great.

1421
00:56:40.310 --> 00:56:45.690
I think that it was really important to Chili's that people know that they are responsible.

1422
00:56:45.990 --> 00:56:47.330
And a family establishment.

1423
00:56:47.430 --> 00:56:48.410
And a family establishment.

1424
00:56:48.690 --> 00:56:54.770
And I love that John Bossert, an actual Chili's, like, owner, got to do that talking head.

1425
00:56:54.870 --> 00:56:56.610
I thought he did a fantastic job.

1426
00:56:56.730 --> 00:56:56.810
He did great.

1427
00:56:56.970 --> 00:56:59.570
His look to camera when he's like, so she is banned.

1428
00:56:59.750 --> 00:57:01.610
Like, his little look to camera was fantastic.

1429
00:57:01.890 --> 00:57:07.650
And also, that aspect of Pam being banned for life was a wonderful thing that just grew into

1430
00:57:07.650 --> 00:57:08.690
many more jokes.

1431
00:57:09.030 --> 00:57:09.710
I know.

1432
00:57:09.850 --> 00:57:10.370
I loved it.

1433
00:57:10.530 --> 00:57:13.870
I love that Pam is, like, such, like, not a troublemaker.

1434
00:57:14.010 --> 00:57:17.170
And she's banned from, like, a nationwide chain.

1435
00:57:17.350 --> 00:57:17.670
Yes.

1436
00:57:18.810 --> 00:57:22.570
As if there is such a system that could control that.

1437
00:57:22.710 --> 00:57:25.350
I have one card that's sort of around that area.

1438
00:57:25.350 --> 00:57:26.810
So can I talk about it right now?

1439
00:57:26.950 --> 00:57:27.290
Sure.

1440
00:57:27.430 --> 00:57:30.350
Once again, Rainn Wilson finds a way to take off his shirt.

1441
00:57:30.450 --> 00:57:32.430
Always taking off his shirt, Rainn Wilson.

1442
00:57:32.450 --> 00:57:34.890
We get to see his beautiful, white, fleshy belly.

1443
00:57:35.090 --> 00:57:36.930
Because somehow, that's going to help save Pam.

1444
00:57:36.930 --> 00:57:38.710
It was going to be a pillow for your head.

1445
00:57:38.910 --> 00:57:39.490
I guess so.

1446
00:57:39.590 --> 00:57:42.090
A lot of people asked about the falling off the stool moment.

1447
00:57:42.270 --> 00:57:43.290
Was it scripted?

1448
00:57:43.430 --> 00:57:44.710
Did I actually do it?

1449
00:57:44.830 --> 00:57:46.010
It was scripted.

1450
00:57:46.110 --> 00:57:47.430
I did actually do it.

1451
00:57:47.590 --> 00:57:52.770
But again, like being drunk, I was very nervous about falling off the stool and making it look

1452
00:57:52.770 --> 00:57:52.990
good.

1453
00:57:53.190 --> 00:57:58.570
So Greg Daniels, he got on the stool, and he showed me how he wanted me to fall.

1454
00:57:58.750 --> 00:58:03.610
He said he wanted me to just keep looking at John and nodding, and then slowly slip off

1455
00:58:03.610 --> 00:58:04.050
the stool.

1456
00:58:04.370 --> 00:58:05.690
And he's very large.

1457
00:58:06.050 --> 00:58:06.330
He's very tall.

1458
00:58:06.330 --> 00:58:06.810
He's tall.

1459
00:58:06.970 --> 00:58:08.090
He's like 6'2 or something.

1460
00:58:08.390 --> 00:58:09.770
And so he fell down.

1461
00:58:09.850 --> 00:58:11.090
They had padding on the floor.

1462
00:58:11.250 --> 00:58:13.750
So he and I were both falling on padding.

1463
00:58:14.270 --> 00:58:20.290
But John, Chris, and Ski and I, we kept pretending like we didn't understand how I should fall

1464
00:58:20.290 --> 00:58:20.830
off the stool.

1465
00:58:21.130 --> 00:58:22.530
On purpose to mess with Greg?

1466
00:58:22.770 --> 00:58:24.750
So that Greg kept doing it?

1467
00:58:24.750 --> 00:58:25.870
He'd have to keep showing us.

1468
00:58:25.950 --> 00:58:26.770
Oh my gosh.

1469
00:58:26.910 --> 00:58:31.110
You were like, that's a moment where you were like real Jim and Pam because you were pranking

1470
00:58:31.110 --> 00:58:33.490
Greg, the way you would prank Dwight.

1471
00:58:33.710 --> 00:58:34.970
A hundred percent.

1472
00:58:35.250 --> 00:58:36.110
Does Greg know that?

1473
00:58:36.370 --> 00:58:36.690
He does.

1474
00:58:37.070 --> 00:58:42.770
And then Greg told me later, I guess John and I told that story in an interview, and he

1475
00:58:42.770 --> 00:58:43.430
confronted us.

1476
00:58:43.550 --> 00:58:45.870
He was like, guys, you know, I really hurt my back doing that.

1477
00:58:45.870 --> 00:58:46.670
No, he did not.

1478
00:58:46.950 --> 00:58:49.410
So we were, then we felt so bad.

1479
00:58:49.890 --> 00:58:50.270
Jenna!

1480
00:58:54.220 --> 00:58:55.860
Oh my God, you guys.

1481
00:58:56.840 --> 00:58:59.360
You, that was real life Jim Pam moment.

1482
00:58:59.520 --> 00:59:00.240
It was.

1483
00:59:00.400 --> 00:59:01.100
It was.

1484
00:59:01.260 --> 00:59:02.480
But I love doing that.

1485
00:59:02.560 --> 00:59:03.820
I love doing that stunt.

1486
00:59:03.980 --> 00:59:05.560
I thought it ended up looking really good too.

1487
00:59:05.700 --> 00:59:06.420
I was proud of it.

1488
00:59:06.540 --> 00:59:07.620
I thought it looked fantastic.

1489
00:59:07.820 --> 00:59:12.280
I thought that whole like part where you were nodding, and then you were like, what?

1490
00:59:12.400 --> 00:59:12.980
And he was like, what?

1491
00:59:13.080 --> 00:59:13.960
And then you start laughing.

1492
00:59:13.960 --> 00:59:15.220
It was so perfect.

1493
00:59:15.500 --> 00:59:16.520
It was so perfect.

1494
00:59:16.800 --> 00:59:20.680
This brings us to the scene with Jim in the parking lot that we were talking about a

1495
00:59:20.680 --> 00:59:21.380
little bit earlier.

1496
00:59:21.740 --> 00:59:25.540
A lot of people wanted to know what was Pam going to ask Jim.

1497
00:59:25.880 --> 00:59:28.460
She wanted to bring up so many things.

1498
00:59:28.600 --> 00:59:29.080
So I think.

1499
00:59:29.200 --> 00:59:34.220
And that's what stopped her because there were so many options going through her head in that

1500
00:59:34.220 --> 00:59:34.500
moment.

1501
00:59:34.720 --> 00:59:40.840
And I had written out in my script all of these things that I could possibly say so that

1502
00:59:40.840 --> 00:59:43.140
I could in that moment rifle through them.

1503
00:59:43.960 --> 00:59:45.560
But then not pick any of them.

1504
00:59:46.540 --> 00:59:51.340
I think it's that moment where you have so much to say, and you're like, can I ask you

1505
00:59:51.340 --> 00:59:51.860
a question?

1506
00:59:52.300 --> 00:59:54.880
And then it would just, the floodgates would have opened.

1507
00:59:55.180 --> 00:59:59.780
But you saw the camera, and it gave you sort of this like check of like, I can't do this.

1508
00:59:59.940 --> 01:00:00.440
Not here.

1509
01:00:00.560 --> 01:00:00.960
Not now.

1510
01:00:01.100 --> 01:00:07.500
And I'm so glad that she didn't because those kind of drunken confessional conversations,

1511
01:00:07.500 --> 01:00:11.020
that wasn't going to lead to the right place.

1512
01:00:11.680 --> 01:00:15.040
You know, I'm glad the camera was there for them in that moment.

1513
01:00:15.500 --> 01:00:19.780
Because I think what Pam was going to say, what I had written in my script was something

1514
01:00:19.780 --> 01:00:22.040
along the lines of, I love you.

1515
01:00:22.340 --> 01:00:26.460
Well, I think the question was going to be, you know, do you think I should break up with

1516
01:00:26.460 --> 01:00:26.720
Roy?

1517
01:00:26.920 --> 01:00:27.220
Yeah.

1518
01:00:27.440 --> 01:00:29.860
What do you, do you think I'm with the wrong person?

1519
01:00:30.080 --> 01:00:30.300
Yeah.

1520
01:00:30.440 --> 01:00:31.380
Those kind of leading questions.

1521
01:00:31.520 --> 01:00:33.320
Hoping that he'd say, you are, be with me.

1522
01:00:33.320 --> 01:00:34.140
Yes, exactly.

1523
01:00:34.980 --> 01:00:36.300
So here's a crazy thing.

1524
01:00:36.400 --> 01:00:42.120
We mentioned earlier that our second season only had six episodes picked up, that this

1525
01:00:42.120 --> 01:00:43.860
was the third episode that we shot.

1526
01:00:44.120 --> 01:00:49.120
And we didn't know this was going to be the premiere of season two when we shot it.

1527
01:00:49.180 --> 01:00:54.580
In fact, one of the ideas was that if we got canceled, it would be the season finale.

1528
01:00:54.580 --> 01:01:03.100
And so I said to Greg, I think just in case we get canceled, and this is the season finale,

1529
01:01:03.420 --> 01:01:10.180
I think we should film an alternate ending to this scene in the parking lot where Pam does

1530
01:01:10.180 --> 01:01:13.340
tell Jim how she feels and they kiss for real.

1531
01:01:13.600 --> 01:01:19.000
Not the Chili's kiss, but the real kiss just so that we could air it and we don't leave

1532
01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:19.720
people hanging.

1533
01:01:21.100 --> 01:01:23.180
And Greg said, no.

1534
01:01:24.600 --> 01:01:25.620
He said, no.

1535
01:01:25.940 --> 01:01:29.740
If they want to see what happens with Jim and Pam, they're just going to have to order

1536
01:01:29.740 --> 01:01:30.660
more episodes.

1537
01:01:31.100 --> 01:01:32.380
I don't want to give them a choice.

1538
01:01:32.660 --> 01:01:33.400
There you go.

1539
01:01:33.520 --> 01:01:35.300
He was very protective of Jim and Pam.

1540
01:01:35.420 --> 01:01:35.860
He was.

1541
01:01:36.060 --> 01:01:38.400
And what went out in the world about that relationship.

1542
01:01:38.720 --> 01:01:42.420
But that shows you how much we thought we were going to be canceled.

1543
01:01:42.740 --> 01:01:42.960
Yeah.

1544
01:01:43.040 --> 01:01:43.580
All the time.

1545
01:01:43.740 --> 01:01:44.240
All the time.

1546
01:01:44.240 --> 01:01:50.080
That I was pitching ideas for how to wrap up the whole series just in case.

1547
01:01:50.380 --> 01:01:55.820
If you think that a normal show gets, well, at that time, network TV, you would get 22

1548
01:01:55.820 --> 01:01:57.260
episodes and we got six.

1549
01:01:57.420 --> 01:02:00.760
It doesn't make you feel like anyone's really confident about what you're doing.

1550
01:02:00.940 --> 01:02:03.940
Like we didn't think NBC was like, oh, we got a winner here.

1551
01:02:04.200 --> 01:02:06.340
I have some deleted scenes cards.

1552
01:02:06.660 --> 01:02:07.620
Oh, tell them.

1553
01:02:07.740 --> 01:02:12.140
Well, one of the ones I really loved is that Toby does a talking head where he says he's never

1554
01:02:12.140 --> 01:02:12.940
won a Dundee.

1555
01:02:12.940 --> 01:02:13.920
Oh, yeah.

1556
01:02:14.220 --> 01:02:16.280
Michael refuses to give Toby a Dundee.

1557
01:02:16.420 --> 01:02:17.560
He just leaves him out every year.

1558
01:02:17.640 --> 01:02:20.560
And now everyone in the office gets a Dundee but Toby.

1559
01:02:20.760 --> 01:02:22.740
And I think, and Toby's like, I'm okay with that.

1560
01:02:22.880 --> 01:02:23.840
I thought that was really funny.

1561
01:02:24.020 --> 01:02:30.000
And then there's a great Dwight Angela scene at the copier where Dwight is really trying

1562
01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:33.420
to force Angela to tell him what was written on the bathroom wall.

1563
01:02:33.700 --> 01:02:35.640
And I'm like, I don't repeat those kind of things.

1564
01:02:35.760 --> 01:02:36.300
It's inappropriate.

1565
01:02:36.300 --> 01:02:37.960
I don't say those words out loud.

1566
01:02:38.120 --> 01:02:41.420
And then Dwight's like, does it have anything to do with his butt or his wiener?

1567
01:02:41.920 --> 01:02:44.120
And I just walk off in a huff.

1568
01:02:44.780 --> 01:02:49.980
But it's the very first time I feel like Dwight and I have some little clandestine conversation

1569
01:02:49.980 --> 01:02:51.220
just between the two of us.

1570
01:02:51.460 --> 01:02:53.060
Oh, that's a good one.

1571
01:02:53.180 --> 01:02:53.340
Yeah.

1572
01:02:53.660 --> 01:02:56.100
Pam does confess that she wrote it on the wall.

1573
01:02:56.200 --> 01:02:56.720
She does.

1574
01:02:56.860 --> 01:02:57.340
About Michael.

1575
01:02:57.440 --> 01:02:59.220
But we don't find out what it was.

1576
01:02:59.280 --> 01:03:00.100
Which I love, too.

1577
01:03:00.300 --> 01:03:02.700
I love what she's like, I feel bad about what I wrote.

1578
01:03:02.740 --> 01:03:03.900
And he's like, no, you don't.

1579
01:03:05.360 --> 01:03:08.680
People wanted to know, did we all get to keep our Dundies?

1580
01:03:09.080 --> 01:03:09.900
Yes, we did.

1581
01:03:10.000 --> 01:03:10.560
Yes, we did.

1582
01:03:10.640 --> 01:03:11.580
We all have them.

1583
01:03:11.740 --> 01:03:12.460
I have two.

1584
01:03:12.680 --> 01:03:14.140
I have two as well.

1585
01:03:14.280 --> 01:03:16.840
I have longest engagement and widest sneakers.

1586
01:03:17.240 --> 01:03:21.440
They gave me the longest engagement that you see me win in earlier years.

1587
01:03:21.600 --> 01:03:23.160
I have the tight ass award.

1588
01:03:23.380 --> 01:03:27.620
And then from years later, which we'll get to, I have the she's kind of a bitch.

1589
01:03:28.120 --> 01:03:31.780
I think Pam doesn't get a Dundie the second time around.

1590
01:03:32.200 --> 01:03:33.140
I don't think so.

1591
01:03:33.340 --> 01:03:34.480
There weren't as many that round.

1592
01:03:34.780 --> 01:03:36.480
I have a final fan question.

1593
01:03:36.780 --> 01:03:38.640
This is something for us to discuss, Angela.

1594
01:03:38.780 --> 01:03:39.660
This is from Samantha.

1595
01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:40.260
Okay.

1596
01:03:40.760 --> 01:03:44.580
She says, the last two times I have watched this episode,

1597
01:03:44.780 --> 01:03:46.980
which is one of my top five favorite episodes,

1598
01:03:47.180 --> 01:03:49.980
we have immediately been hit by a tornado.

1599
01:03:50.380 --> 01:03:54.100
Within 10 minutes of the line, I feel God in this Chili's tonight.

1600
01:03:54.280 --> 01:03:56.200
Samantha, first of all, where do you live?

1601
01:03:56.200 --> 01:03:59.040
Do you think I'm jinxed or is it just bad luck?

1602
01:03:59.520 --> 01:04:01.840
Should Samantha ever watch this episode again?

1603
01:04:02.060 --> 01:04:04.400
I would say, do you live in Tornado Alley?

1604
01:04:04.580 --> 01:04:07.300
Do you live in like Kansas, North Texas, Oklahoma?

1605
01:04:07.680 --> 01:04:09.380
Like where, where do you live?

1606
01:04:09.480 --> 01:04:09.740
Right.

1607
01:04:10.100 --> 01:04:13.260
And perhaps the next time you watch it, watch it in the storm cellar?

1608
01:04:13.560 --> 01:04:16.620
Or maybe hit pause right before that line.

1609
01:04:16.980 --> 01:04:17.840
Check the weather.

1610
01:04:18.380 --> 01:04:18.900
Skip it.

1611
01:04:19.160 --> 01:04:20.740
Just skip ahead and watch the end.

1612
01:04:20.740 --> 01:04:21.300
And come back.

1613
01:04:21.420 --> 01:04:22.740
That is a crazy coincidence.

1614
01:04:22.740 --> 01:04:23.460
That is crazy.

1615
01:04:23.640 --> 01:04:25.320
That was the craziest fan question we got.

1616
01:04:25.320 --> 01:04:28.200
I had to include it because I found it so charming.

1617
01:04:28.240 --> 01:04:29.460
And I was a little worried about Samantha.

1618
01:04:29.980 --> 01:04:30.860
That was it.

1619
01:04:31.020 --> 01:04:32.040
That's the Dundies.

1620
01:04:32.060 --> 01:04:33.480
That is the Dundies.

1621
01:04:33.660 --> 01:04:36.120
And next week, we will be talking about sexual harassment.

1622
01:04:36.360 --> 01:04:37.800
The episode sexual harassment.

1623
01:04:38.040 --> 01:04:38.240
Correct.

1624
01:04:38.420 --> 01:04:41.600
We will be talking about the episode sexual harassment.

1625
01:04:41.860 --> 01:04:42.480
All right, you guys.

1626
